1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:10,008
What's Today's Video About? Summer Travel Picks: Hokkaido or Okinawa?

2
00:00:10,008 --> 00:00:13,008
Scene 1: Summer Travel Destinations – Hokkaido or Okinawa

3
00:00:13,008 --> 00:00:17,977
Let’s plan this summer’s trip!

4
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:20,634
Sounds great!

5
00:00:20,657 --> 00:00:25,204
Hokkaido or Okinawa would be perfect.

6
00:00:25,227 --> 00:00:28,702
Which one is more popular?

7
00:00:28,726 --> 00:00:34,959
Both are famous summer destinations.

8
00:00:34,982 --> 00:00:39,615
Is Hokkaido cool in the summer?

9
00:00:39,638 --> 00:00:45,738
Yes, it’s much cooler than Tokyo.

10
00:00:45,761 --> 00:00:49,912
The temperature is around 25°C (77°F).

11
00:00:49,936 --> 00:00:54,046
That’s really comfortable!

12
00:00:54,069 --> 00:00:57,538
How about Okinawa?

13
00:00:57,561 --> 00:01:01,996
Okinawa is hot.

14
00:01:02,020 --> 00:01:06,724
The temperature gets up to around 32°C (90°F).

15
00:01:06,748 --> 00:01:10,667
32°C is pretty hot!

16
00:01:10,691 --> 00:01:15,275
But the ocean is stunning.

17
00:01:15,298 --> 00:01:17,767
That’s true.

18
00:01:17,790 --> 00:01:22,502
The blue sea is absolutely breathtaking.

19
00:01:22,526 --> 00:01:27,226
Doesn’t Hokkaido have an ocean?

20
00:01:27,249 --> 00:01:31,806
Hokkaido has an ocean too.

21
00:01:31,829 --> 00:01:36,330
But not many people swim there.

22
00:01:36,353 --> 00:01:39,744
Is the water cold?

23
00:01:39,768 --> 00:01:42,242
Yes.

24
00:01:42,265 --> 00:01:45,932
It’s a little chilly even in summer.

25
00:01:45,955 --> 00:01:49,422
Got it.

26
00:01:49,445 --> 00:01:53,578
Is Okinawa’s ocean warm?

27
00:01:53,601 --> 00:01:58,919
Yes, you can swim until September.

28
00:01:58,942 --> 00:02:03,700
The weather and ocean are totally different!

29
00:02:03,724 --> 00:02:05,881
Exactly.

30
00:02:05,904 --> 00:02:09,441
The food is different too.

31
00:02:09,465 --> 00:02:13,171
What kind of food do they have?

32
00:02:13,194 --> 00:02:18,150
Hokkaido has delicious seafood.

33
00:02:18,173 --> 00:02:22,606
Okinawa has mangoes.

34
00:02:22,629 --> 00:02:26,529
Both sound amazing!

35
00:02:26,552 --> 00:02:33,657
Check the description and top comment for a link to review today’s video! *Note: The site may be removed without notice.

36
00:02:33,657 --> 00:02:36,657
Scene 2: Exploring Famous Spots in Japan

37
00:02:36,657 --> 00:02:42,366
Let’s look up famous places on the computer.

38
00:02:42,390 --> 00:02:47,823
First, let’s check out famous spots in Hokkaido.

39
00:02:47,846 --> 00:02:52,351
Sapporo and Otaru are well-known.

40
00:02:52,375 --> 00:02:57,849
Yes, Furano’s lavender fields are beautiful too.

41
00:02:57,873 --> 00:03:01,808
Those purple flowers, right?

42
00:03:01,832 --> 00:03:04,698
I’ve seen photos.

43
00:03:04,721 --> 00:03:08,155
They’re so gorgeous!

44
00:03:08,178 --> 00:03:13,318
Biei’s Blue Pond is also popular.

45
00:03:13,341 --> 00:03:17,861
The water is such a vivid blue!

46
00:03:17,884 --> 00:03:20,857
It’s a magical place.

47
00:03:20,881 --> 00:03:25,914
There’s also Asahiyama Zoo.

48
00:03:25,937 --> 00:03:29,370
The animals feel so close!

49
00:03:29,393 --> 00:03:33,093
Hokkaido is huge!

50
00:03:33,116 --> 00:03:37,150
There are so many places I want to visit!

51
00:03:37,173 --> 00:03:42,083
Next, let's explore Okinawa.

52
00:03:42,106 --> 00:03:46,842
Naha's International Street is famous.

53
00:03:46,865 --> 00:03:52,532
Yes! It's the ultimate spot for lively shopping.

54
00:03:52,555 --> 00:03:56,288
Shuri Castle is also well-known.

55
00:03:56,311 --> 00:03:59,686
It's a striking red building.

56
00:03:59,709 --> 00:04:02,267
That’s true.

57
00:04:02,291 --> 00:04:05,964
A historic site of Okinawa's past.

58
00:04:05,987 --> 00:04:09,895
What about aquariums?

59
00:04:09,919 --> 00:04:13,953
There's the Churaumi Aquarium.

60
00:04:13,977 --> 00:04:18,482
It's one of the largest in the world!

61
00:04:18,505 --> 00:04:22,291
And they have huge sharks!

62
00:04:22,315 --> 00:04:27,148
Yes! Whale sharks swimming around.

63
00:04:27,171 --> 00:04:31,323
Kouri Island's beaches are stunning too.

64
00:04:31,347 --> 00:04:35,662
You drive across a long bridge to get there.

65
00:04:35,685 --> 00:04:39,118
The views are absolutely breathtaking.

66
00:04:39,141 --> 00:04:44,779
Both places are so famous—it's hard to choose!

67
00:04:44,803 --> 00:04:47,874
Totally!

68
00:04:47,898 --> 00:04:51,798
It's such a tough decision.

69
00:04:51,821 --> 00:04:57,626
Let me know in the comments if you caught all that!

70
00:04:57,626 --> 00:05:00,626
Scene 3: Summer Vacation Travel Plans

71
00:05:00,626 --> 00:05:07,259
I just can't give up on Hokkaido or Okinawa.

72
00:05:07,282 --> 00:05:10,315
Same here!

73
00:05:10,338 --> 00:05:13,605
I want to visit both.

74
00:05:13,628 --> 00:05:17,861
Then let's go to both!

75
00:05:17,884 --> 00:05:20,518
Really?

76
00:05:20,541 --> 00:05:23,614
We're visiting both?

77
00:05:23,637 --> 00:05:25,871
Yes.

78
00:05:25,893 --> 00:05:30,160
This year's summer break is long.

79
00:05:30,183 --> 00:05:33,132
We have two whole weeks!

80
00:05:33,156 --> 00:05:37,489
Two weeks is amazing!

81
00:05:37,512 --> 00:05:41,279
We have plenty of time.

82
00:05:41,302 --> 00:05:46,606
Let's spend the first week in Hokkaido.

83
00:05:46,630 --> 00:05:49,336
Sounds great!

84
00:05:49,360 --> 00:05:53,112
Starting with a cool destination.

85
00:05:53,136 --> 00:05:58,202
Then we'll return to Tokyo once.

86
00:05:58,225 --> 00:06:02,294
After that, off to Okinawa!

87
00:06:02,318 --> 00:06:05,784
That's the perfect plan!

88
00:06:05,807 --> 00:06:09,401
Let's book our flights.

89
00:06:09,425 --> 00:06:13,997
Summer tickets are affordable right now.

90
00:06:14,020 --> 00:06:17,120
We should book early.

91
00:06:17,143 --> 00:06:20,410
Let's look for hotels too.

92
00:06:20,433 --> 00:06:24,333
Hotels in Sapporo and Naha.

93
00:06:24,356 --> 00:06:28,623
A hotel near the station would be great.

94
00:06:28,646 --> 00:06:32,746
Yeah, it makes getting around so much easier.

95
00:06:32,769 --> 00:06:36,888
Do we need a rental car?

96
00:06:36,911 --> 00:06:39,044
Yes.

97
00:06:39,067 --> 00:06:42,934
We'll use it in Furano and Kouri Island.

98
00:06:42,957 --> 00:06:47,109
I'll drive!

99
00:06:47,132 --> 00:06:49,832
Thank you!

100
00:06:49,855 --> 00:06:53,589
I'll handle the navigation.

101
00:06:53,612 --> 00:06:57,878
This is going to be such a fun trip!

102
00:06:57,901 --> 00:06:59,881
Yes.

103
00:06:59,904 --> 00:07:02,973
Let's hurry and get everything ready!

104
00:07:02,996 --> 00:07:05,996
Scene 4: Exploring Sapporo and Otaru

105
00:07:05,996 --> 00:07:09,937
We've arrived in Sapporo!

106
00:07:09,961 --> 00:07:14,337
The air is so fresh here.

107
00:07:14,361 --> 00:07:18,927
Let's take a walk through Odori Park.

108
00:07:18,950 --> 00:07:23,117
There's so much greenery.

109
00:07:23,140 --> 00:07:28,898
Look, there's the TV Tower over there.

110
00:07:28,922 --> 00:07:31,704
It's really tall.

111
00:07:31,727 --> 00:07:36,594
The Clock Tower is nearby too.

112
00:07:36,617 --> 00:07:40,252
It's a historic building.

113
00:07:40,276 --> 00:07:46,475
Sapporo is such a clean and walkable city.

114
00:07:46,498 --> 00:07:51,965
Now, let's head to Otaru by train.

115
00:07:51,988 --> 00:07:55,145
It only takes thirty minutes.

116
00:07:55,169 --> 00:07:58,869
We've arrived in Otaru.

117
00:07:58,892 --> 00:08:03,370
There are so many old warehouses here.

118
00:08:03,393 --> 00:08:07,893
This is the Otaru Canal.

119
00:08:07,916 --> 00:08:11,416
The gas lamps are so beautiful.

120
00:08:11,439 --> 00:08:15,672
It's such a romantic view.

121
00:08:15,695 --> 00:08:19,772
This is the exact spot from the photos.

122
00:08:19,795 --> 00:08:24,262
At night, it's all lit up.

123
00:08:24,285 --> 00:08:27,664
It becomes even more stunning.

124
00:08:27,687 --> 00:08:31,633
I'm getting hungry.

125
00:08:31,657 --> 00:08:35,490
Let's grab something delicious to eat.

126
00:08:35,513 --> 00:08:39,883
Otaru is famous for its sushi.

127
00:08:39,906 --> 00:08:43,459
I know a great place.

128
00:08:43,483 --> 00:08:48,858
I'd love to try the seafood bowl.

129
00:08:48,881 --> 00:08:53,381
It's packed with crab and uni.

130
00:08:53,404 --> 00:08:58,537
This restaurant's seafood bowl is legendary.

131
00:08:58,560 --> 00:09:02,693
The fish is incredibly fresh.

132
00:09:02,716 --> 00:09:05,616
Let's dig in!

133
00:09:05,639 --> 00:09:10,906
Wow, the uni is so sweet!

134
00:09:10,929 --> 00:09:15,476
And the crab is so meaty.

135
00:09:15,500 --> 00:09:18,800
This is amazing.

136
00:09:18,823 --> 00:09:23,523
It's nothing like the fish in Tokyo.

137
00:09:23,546 --> 00:09:29,846
The waters in Hokkaido are cold.

138
00:09:29,869 --> 00:09:34,185
That's why the fish tastes so good.

139
00:09:34,208 --> 00:09:38,975
We got to enjoy such delicious food on our first day.

140
00:09:38,998 --> 00:09:43,931
I can't wait for tomorrow's adventure.

141
00:09:43,954 --> 00:09:46,954
Scene 5: Scenic Drive in Furano and Biei

142
00:09:46,954 --> 00:09:52,621
Today, we're going on a drive with a rental car.

143
00:09:52,644 --> 00:09:56,310
We've arrived in Furano.

144
00:09:56,333 --> 00:10:01,682
The lavender fields are right in front of us.

145
00:10:01,706 --> 00:10:05,373
It's incredible!

146
00:10:05,396 --> 00:10:09,662
The mountains are completely purple.

147
00:10:09,685 --> 00:10:13,592
And it smells so good too.

148
00:10:13,616 --> 00:10:17,322
The breeze feels wonderful.

149
00:10:17,346 --> 00:10:22,048
Let's try Furano's famous melon.

150
00:10:22,072 --> 00:10:24,551
Yes.

151
00:10:24,574 --> 00:10:29,358
Furano melons are so sweet.

152
00:10:29,382 --> 00:10:33,349
They're bursting with juice.

153
00:10:33,372 --> 00:10:36,872
It's delicious!

154
00:10:36,895 --> 00:10:42,962
Next, let's head to the Blue Pond in Biei.

155
00:10:42,985 --> 00:10:46,251
We've arrived in Biei.

156
00:10:46,274 --> 00:10:50,308
There's a beautiful row of trees.

157
00:10:50,331 --> 00:10:55,164
There's a pond over there.

158
00:10:55,187 --> 00:10:57,731
Look at that!

159
00:10:57,754 --> 00:11:04,188
Wow, the water is so blue!

160
00:11:04,211 --> 00:11:07,796
Like paint blue.

161
00:11:07,819 --> 00:11:10,758
It's magical, isn't it?

162
00:11:10,782 --> 00:11:16,378
There's a white tree standing in the pond.

163
00:11:16,402 --> 00:11:21,757
This tree is dead, isn't it?

164
00:11:21,780 --> 00:11:26,058
It's just like the one by the bed.

165
00:11:26,081 --> 00:11:31,255
The color changes with the sunlight.

166
00:11:31,279 --> 00:11:35,626
It's the most beautiful right now.

167
00:11:35,650 --> 00:11:40,283
So many people are taking photos.

168
00:11:40,306 --> 00:11:45,806
Let's take a photo together.

169
00:11:45,829 --> 00:11:48,462
Yes.

170
00:11:48,485 --> 00:11:52,619
Let's take it by the pond.

171
00:11:52,643 --> 00:11:56,421
We got a great shot!

172
00:11:56,444 --> 00:11:59,434
This will be a wonderful keepsake.

173
00:11:59,457 --> 00:12:05,527
The nature in Furano and Biei is breathtaking.

174
00:12:05,550 --> 00:12:11,384
Yes, driving through Hokkaido is amazing.

175
00:12:11,407 --> 00:12:14,407
Scene 6: The Charm of Asahiyama Zoo

176
00:12:14,407 --> 00:12:18,002
We've arrived in Asahikawa.

177
00:12:18,025 --> 00:12:22,573
Let's head into Asahiyama Zoo.

178
00:12:22,596 --> 00:12:28,793
This zoo is famous for its unique design.

179
00:12:28,816 --> 00:12:33,283
Oh, there's the penguin pool!

180
00:12:33,306 --> 00:12:38,041
We can see them from below.

181
00:12:38,064 --> 00:12:41,374
Let's go into the tunnel.

182
00:12:41,397 --> 00:12:44,630
It's incredible!

183
00:12:44,653 --> 00:12:48,320
The penguins look like they're flying in the air!

184
00:12:48,343 --> 00:12:53,710
They swim so fast underwater.

185
00:12:53,733 --> 00:12:56,712
Just like birds!

186
00:12:56,735 --> 00:13:01,402
Next up is the polar bear exhibit.

187
00:13:01,425 --> 00:13:06,208
The bear just roared loudly!

188
00:13:06,231 --> 00:13:10,664
It's diving into the water!

189
00:13:10,687 --> 00:13:14,354
The splash is coming this way!

190
00:13:14,377 --> 00:13:17,490
That was incredible!

191
00:13:17,514 --> 00:13:22,654
There's also a cylindrical pool for the seals.

192
00:13:22,677 --> 00:13:27,473
Oh, a seal just swam through vertically!

193
00:13:27,497 --> 00:13:31,849
They glide so smoothly.

194
00:13:31,872 --> 00:13:34,572
This is so fun!

195
00:13:34,595 --> 00:13:39,962
The animals are so lively—it's a joy to watch.

196
00:13:39,985 --> 00:13:43,718
We've been walking for three hours.

197
00:13:43,741 --> 00:13:47,260
I'm a little tired.

198
00:13:47,284 --> 00:13:53,550
Let's go try Asahikawa's famous ramen.

199
00:13:53,573 --> 00:13:57,943
There's a well-known shop for soy sauce ramen.

200
00:13:57,967 --> 00:14:02,564
The warm soup is delicious.

201
00:14:02,587 --> 00:14:05,854
The noodles are wavy.

202
00:14:05,877 --> 00:14:09,810
The chashu is so tender.

203
00:14:09,833 --> 00:14:13,700
I'm stuffed!

204
00:14:13,723 --> 00:14:18,856
Our last day in Hokkaido was perfect.

205
00:14:18,879 --> 00:14:24,032
Tomorrow, we head back to Tokyo.

206
00:14:24,055 --> 00:14:27,055
Scene 7: The Start of an Okinawan Trip

207
00:14:27,055 --> 00:14:31,201
We've arrived at Naha Airport.

208
00:14:31,225 --> 00:14:34,730
It's so hot here!

209
00:14:34,754 --> 00:14:37,143
Yes.

210
00:14:37,166 --> 00:14:43,533
Okinawa's summer sun is intense!

211
00:14:43,556 --> 00:14:47,549
The blue sky is stunning.

212
00:14:47,573 --> 00:14:52,639
Let's start with Kokusai Street.

213
00:14:52,662 --> 00:14:58,002
There are so many souvenir shops here.

214
00:14:58,026 --> 00:15:02,659
Look, Okinawan sweets!

215
00:15:02,682 --> 00:15:06,467
I want to buy some *chinsuko*.

216
00:15:06,491 --> 00:15:11,524
The purple sweet potato tarts are delicious too!

217
00:15:11,547 --> 00:15:16,181
There are so many unique things here.

218
00:15:16,204 --> 00:15:19,704
You won’t get tired of browsing.

219
00:15:19,727 --> 00:15:24,309
I’m getting hungry—it’s lunchtime!

220
00:15:24,332 --> 00:15:27,999
Let’s have Okinawan soba.

221
00:15:28,022 --> 00:15:32,688
Is it a bit different from ramen?

222
00:15:32,711 --> 00:15:38,611
Yeah, it has white noodles like udon.

223
00:15:38,634 --> 00:15:42,968
And it comes with big slices of pork on top.

224
00:15:42,991 --> 00:15:48,857
The broth is light and so tasty!

225
00:15:48,880 --> 00:15:54,755
Adding red pickled ginger changes the flavor.

226
00:15:54,779 --> 00:15:57,812
Totally!

227
00:15:57,835 --> 00:16:00,969
It makes it really refreshing.

228
00:16:00,992 --> 00:16:05,825
Next, let’s head to Shuri Castle.

229
00:16:05,848 --> 00:16:09,805
There’s the gate of Shuri Castle!

230
00:16:09,828 --> 00:16:13,261
It’s huge!

231
00:16:13,284 --> 00:16:17,551
The whole building is red, isn’t it?

232
00:16:17,574 --> 00:16:21,607
It shows Chinese influence.

233
00:16:21,630 --> 00:16:26,786
It’s totally different from other Japanese castles.

234
00:16:26,810 --> 00:16:33,543
Yeah, you can feel the history of the Ryukyu Kingdom.

235
00:16:33,566 --> 00:16:39,108
From up here, you can see Naha’s ocean.

236
00:16:39,131 --> 00:16:42,198
The view is amazing.

237
00:16:42,221 --> 00:16:48,254
Our first day of sightseeing in Okinawa was so fun!

238
00:16:48,277 --> 00:16:51,277
Scene 8: The Giant Whale Shark at the Aquarium

239
00:16:51,277 --> 00:16:55,944
We’ve arrived at Churaumi Aquarium.

240
00:16:55,967 --> 00:16:59,839
The building is massive!

241
00:16:59,862 --> 00:17:05,329
Let’s go to the biggest tank.

242
00:17:05,352 --> 00:17:09,819
It’s called the Kuroshio Sea.

243
00:17:09,842 --> 00:17:15,839
Wow, the water is so blue—it’s right in front of us!

244
00:17:15,862 --> 00:17:19,405
It’s like a movie theater!

245
00:17:19,428 --> 00:17:25,214
Look, there’s a huge whale shark over there!

246
00:17:25,237 --> 00:17:29,471
It’s enormous!

247
00:17:29,494 --> 00:17:33,927
Is it ten meters long?

248
00:17:33,950 --> 00:17:39,453
Yes, even longer than ten meters.

249
00:17:39,476 --> 00:17:43,190
It weighs nine tons.

250
00:17:43,214 --> 00:17:46,757
Nine tons?!

251
00:17:46,781 --> 00:17:51,535
It’s the biggest fish in the world!

252
00:17:51,559 --> 00:17:54,870
That’s true.

253
00:17:54,893 --> 00:18:00,359
It eats thirty kilograms of tiny shrimp every day.

254
00:18:00,382 --> 00:18:05,449
Thirty kilograms of food—that’s a lot!

255
00:18:05,472 --> 00:18:11,572
Next to the whale shark, manta rays are swimming too!

256
00:18:11,595 --> 00:18:15,862
Those are reef manta rays.

257
00:18:15,886 --> 00:18:21,429
They’re black and glide through the water like they’re flying.

258
00:18:21,452 --> 00:18:25,486
Their movements are so graceful.

259
00:18:25,509 --> 00:18:29,176
They’re beautiful.

260
00:18:29,199 --> 00:18:35,032
Below them, sharks and rays are resting on the bottom.

261
00:18:35,055 --> 00:18:40,011
There are also lots of deep-sea fish down there!

262
00:18:40,035 --> 00:18:42,705
It's glowing.

263
00:18:42,729 --> 00:18:48,462
I could watch this pool forever and never get tired of it.

264
00:18:48,485 --> 00:18:53,352
Yes. There are seats with chairs.

265
00:18:53,375 --> 00:18:56,684
Let's sit here.

266
00:18:56,708 --> 00:19:01,301
What a beautiful blue world.

267
00:19:01,324 --> 00:19:03,910
It's so soothing.

268
00:19:03,934 --> 00:19:10,113
Okinawa's aquarium is truly amazing.

269
00:19:10,136 --> 00:19:15,452
Absolutely. I could stay here all day.

270
00:19:15,476 --> 00:19:21,154
Now, let's check out the souvenir corner.

271
00:19:21,177 --> 00:19:24,177
Scene 9: Drive and Beach at Kouri Island

272
00:19:24,177 --> 00:19:30,210
Today, we're driving to Kouri Island.

273
00:19:30,233 --> 00:19:34,428
I see the long bridge ahead!

274
00:19:34,452 --> 00:19:38,918
This is the bridge to Kouri Island.

275
00:19:38,941 --> 00:19:43,609
Look at the ocean on both sides of the bridge.

276
00:19:43,633 --> 00:19:47,100
It's emerald green.

277
00:19:47,123 --> 00:19:51,315
It's absolutely stunning.

278
00:19:51,339 --> 00:19:57,256
It feels like we're driving on the ocean.

279
00:19:57,279 --> 00:20:00,858
We've arrived at the island.

280
00:20:00,881 --> 00:20:03,848
Let's head to the beach.

281
00:20:03,872 --> 00:20:08,856
The white sand is so fine.

282
00:20:08,879 --> 00:20:11,986
Let's walk barefoot.

283
00:20:12,009 --> 00:20:15,968
It feels amazing.

284
00:20:15,992 --> 00:20:19,747
The water is so clear.

285
00:20:19,770 --> 00:20:23,804
Let's dip our feet in the water.

286
00:20:23,827 --> 00:20:28,927
It's a little cold, but it feels great.

287
00:20:28,950 --> 00:20:34,816
Look, there's a heart-shaped rock in the distance.

288
00:20:34,839 --> 00:20:40,373
That's a famous power spot.

289
00:20:40,396 --> 00:20:43,529
Let's take some photos.

290
00:20:43,552 --> 00:20:45,752
Yes.

291
00:20:45,775 --> 00:20:49,972
The sound of the waves is so relaxing.

292
00:20:49,996 --> 00:20:54,562
The sun is really strong.

293
00:20:54,585 --> 00:20:57,485
We're going to get a tan.

294
00:20:57,508 --> 00:21:02,077
Let's grab a cold juice.

295
00:21:02,101 --> 00:21:05,134
There's a shop over there.

296
00:21:05,157 --> 00:21:10,132
It's pineapple juice from Okinawa.

297
00:21:10,156 --> 00:21:14,656
It's tangy and so sweet.

298
00:21:14,679 --> 00:21:17,312
It's revitalizing.

299
00:21:17,335 --> 00:21:23,669
Spending time on the beach like this is such a luxury.

300
00:21:23,692 --> 00:21:30,880
Yes. It makes me forget about the busy life in Tokyo.

301
00:21:30,903 --> 00:21:37,496
Okinawa's nature really rejuvenates our spirits.

302
00:21:37,520 --> 00:21:42,904
I'm so glad we came to this island.

303
00:21:42,927 --> 00:21:50,470
Absolutely. Let's wait for the beautiful evening scenery.

304
00:21:50,494 --> 00:21:53,494
Scene 10: Memories of the Trip

305
00:21:53,494 --> 00:21:57,061
Our trip has come to an end.

306
00:21:57,085 --> 00:22:00,918
We're back in Tokyo.

307
00:22:00,941 --> 00:22:02,974
Yes.

308
00:22:02,997 --> 00:22:09,147
Those two weeks in Hokkaido and Okinawa flew by.

309
00:22:09,171 --> 00:22:14,675
We made so many wonderful memories.

310
00:22:14,699 --> 00:22:19,965
Which place did you like the most?

311
00:22:19,988 --> 00:22:24,422
I can't choose.

312
00:22:24,445 --> 00:22:27,911
Both were incredible.

313
00:22:27,934 --> 00:22:32,468
What's your favorite memory from Hokkaido?

314
00:22:32,491 --> 00:22:37,924
The vibrant purple lavender fields of Furano.

315
00:22:37,947 --> 00:22:40,895
The scenery was absolutely stunning.

316
00:22:40,918 --> 00:22:47,152
The penguins at Asahiyama Zoo were so much fun, right?

317
00:22:47,175 --> 00:22:49,052
Yeah, they were!

318
00:22:49,076 --> 00:22:54,109
The seafood and ramen were incredibly delicious too.

319
00:22:54,132 --> 00:22:58,232
How about your memories of Okinawa?

320
00:22:58,255 --> 00:23:03,733
The massive whale shark at Churaumi Aquarium.

321
00:23:03,757 --> 00:23:07,098
It was so impressive!

322
00:23:07,122 --> 00:23:12,455
The crystal-clear blue ocean at Kouri Island was breathtaking too.

323
00:23:12,478 --> 00:23:14,797
Yes.

324
00:23:14,821 --> 00:23:19,763
I can't forget the juice I had on that pristine white beach.

325
00:23:19,786 --> 00:23:28,252
We experienced both the cool nature of the north and the warm seas of the south.

326
00:23:28,275 --> 00:23:32,650
What a luxurious summer trip that was!

327
00:23:32,674 --> 00:23:34,741
Yeah, they were!

328
00:23:34,764 --> 00:23:40,515
We took so many photos—let’s make an album!

329
00:23:40,539 --> 00:23:43,129
Sounds great!

330
00:23:43,152 --> 00:23:46,820
I want to show them to my friends too.

331
00:23:46,844 --> 00:23:51,744
Where should we go next summer?

332
00:23:51,766 --> 00:23:56,600
Let’s plan another trip to a new place!

333
00:23:56,623 --> 00:23:58,957
Yes.

334
00:23:58,980 --> 00:24:04,219
Let’s work hard and go on another adventure next time!